{"id":"000W7W","title":"Lichtenburg Figure (collab with Ambrose)","author":"damo_89","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-26T01:48:44+00:00","posted":"Gestern, 19:55 Uhr","rules":"This puzzle was set as part of an event with the Skunkworks where each participant was randomly assigned a setting partner, except all communication was done anonymously through a chatbot, and neither partner knew who their setting partner was until the puzzle was set and the competition ended. I was unknowingly paired with Ambrose and I had an absolute pleasure setting this puzzle. I hope you have as much pleasure solving.\n\n• Normal sudoku rules apply.\n\n• Yin Yang: Shade each cell one of two colors in such a way that, for each color the cells of that color form a single region connected by shared edges, and no 2x2 square is a single color.\n\n• Ambiguous kropki: A dot on an edge indicates that the digits in the cells it touches are: consecutive if the cells have different colors; and in a 1 to 2 ratio if the cells have the same color. (A 1-2 pair on a dot can be the either the same or different colors). No negative constraint.\n\nPlay on Sudokupad","solutionCode":"Digits in cells with the same color as R1C1 in row 7","tags":["Sudoku","Yin und Yang","Kropki Pairs (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/53fmahs4dg","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/53fmahs4dg","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-26T01:48:44+00:00"}